```javascript
export function getMochaTestPath(runnable) {
  const path = [];
  let node;
  if (runnable.type === 'hook') {
    node = runnable.ctx.currentTest;
  } else {
    node = runnable;
  }

  while (node && node.parent) {
    if (node.title) {
      path.push(node.title);
    }
    node = node.parent;
  }
  return path.reverse();
}
```

This function builds an array representing the path to a Mocha test. It starts by determining the initial `node`: if the runnable is a hook, it uses `runnable.ctx.currentTest`; otherwise it uses the runnable directly. It then walks up the parent chain, collecting each node's title, and finally reverses the array so the path reads from the outermost parent to the test itself.

